#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/alpha.md:19
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/beta1.md:18
msgid "En route to the new Plasma, Frameworks and Gear"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/alpha.md:21
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/beta1.md:20
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/beta2.md:21
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/rc1.md:21
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/rc2.md:21
msgid "Every few years we port the key components of our software to a new version of [Qt](https://www.qt.io/product/qt6), taking the opportunity to remove cruft and leverage the updated features the most recent version of Qt has to offer us."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/alpha.md:23
msgid "It has been nearly 10 years since the last big release of our flagship Plasma desktop environment, and the time has come again. KDE is making available today the [Alpha](#alpha) version of all the software we will include in a megarelease scheduled for **the end of February 2024**."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/alpha.md:25
msgid "To ensure all parts of KDE's software stack are working together, we are releasing all our major bundles at the same time. Today sees the start of that journey with the Alpha releases of Plasma 6, KDE Frameworks 6 and the KDE Gear bundle of apps."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/alpha.md:27
msgid "For more on what we mean when we talk about \"Alpha Software\", see the [What is Alpha software](#alpha) section below. But, to summarize, this is a very early preview intended for developers and testers only. We hope it will be picked up by rolling unstable distros, but it is far from being ready for day-to-day use yet."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/alpha.md:29
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/beta1.md:28
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/beta2.md:29
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/rc1.md:29
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/rc2.md:29
msgid "Read on to find out more about KDE's 6th Megarelease, what it covers, and how [you can help make the new versions of Plasma, KDE's apps and Frameworks a success](#contributing) now."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/alpha.md:31
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/beta1.md:30
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/beta2.md:31
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/rc1.md:31
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/rc2.md:31
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Plasma Next"
msgid "[Plasma](/plasma-desktop/)"
msgstr "Plasma Next"

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/alpha.md:33
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/beta1.md:32
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/beta2.md:33
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/rc1.md:33
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/rc2.md:33
msgid "Plasma is KDE's flagship desktop environment. Plasma is like Windows or macOS, but is renowned for being flexible, powerful, lightweight and configurable. It can be used at home, at work, for schools and research."
