#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Kdenlive and Okular"
msgid "Konsole and Yakuake"
msgstr "Kdenlive e Okular"

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/index.md:0
msgid ""
"In Gear 24.02, apart from being ported to Qt 6, we redesigned the settings of\n"
"Konsole, and Yakuake and Konsole's rendering is now more performant with\n"
"[50% fewer memory allocations](https://invent.kde.org/utilities/konsole/-/merge_requests/913).\n"
"\n"
"People using Konsole with Chinese, Japanese, or Korean scripts will be happy\n"
"to hear that text selection is now working correctly.\n"
"\n"
"Konsole now puts every tab in a separate [cgroup](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cgroups).\n"
"This avoids the entire application getting killed when the system is suffering\n"
"from high memory load and needs to save some memory by terminating processes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/index.md:0
msgid "But wait, there's even more"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/index.md:0
msgid "KClock"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/index.md:0
msgid ""
"KClock will pause any media sources (media players, streaming services,\n"
"etc.) when an alarm or timer rings, and then resume them when the alarm\n"
"is dismissed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/megarelease/6/index.md:0
msgid ""
"KDE Connect can now connect to other devices via Bluetooth. This may be\n"
"less reliable than the current Wi-Fi backend, but can be useful when your two\n"
"devices are not connected to the same Wi-Fi network or when are separated\n"
"by a firewall.\n"
"\n"
"In terms of discoverability, KDE Connect now also\n"
"supports [mDNS](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multicast_DNS) which is\n"
"better at finding other devices in your network and less often blocked\n"
"by the network configuration.\n"
msgstr ""

