#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:45
msgid "The new launcher features two panes to make it simple to locate your programs and comes with improved keyboard, mouse, and touch input, boosting accessibility across the board."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:49
msgid "Support for languages with right-to-left writing (such as Japanese and Arabic) has also improved. We have also included an alphabetical \"All Applications\" view, a grid view for your favorite tools, and placed all the power actions (\"Sleep\", \"Restart\", \"Shut Down\", etc.) at the bottom of the launcher pop-up so they are always visible and available."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:56
msgid "If you prefer the old Kickoff app launcher however, it is only few clicks away in [KDE's software store](https://store.kde.org)."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:65
msgid "Continuing with improvements to the look and feel, applications using Plasma's default theme now have a refreshed color scheme and sport a brand new unified headerbar style with a clean, cool new look."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:79
msgid "Meet Breeze Twilight: a combination of a dark theme for Plasma and a light theme for applications, so you can enjoy the best of both worlds. Find it in the Global Theme section of your Settings"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:94
msgid "Plasma System Monitor provides a wide variety of different views, offering an overview page with information on important core resources, such as memory, disk space, network and CPU usage. It also provides a quick view of the applications consuming the most resources. This lets you easily locate and zap applications or processes that are slowing your computer down."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:100
msgid "If you need more details, the Applications page shows you all the running applications along with detailed statistics and graphs. A process page is also available for per-process information, and History shows the evolution of the use of your machine's resources over time."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:105
msgid "Finally, you can also create your own new customized pages using the page editor. This lets you tailor the information you get from your system to your needs."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:126
msgid "KDE is pushing to have first class support for Wayland, and Plasma 5.21 makes massive progress towards reaching that goal."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:129
msgid "We have extensively refactored the compositing code in KWin and the changes should reduce latency throughout all compositing operations. We have also added a control in the compositing settings so you can choose whether you prefer lower latency or smoother animations."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:134
msgid "In addition, we have also added support for mixed-refresh-rate display setups on Wayland, e.g. you can have one screen refreshing at 144Hz and another at 60Hz, which is ideal for improving work-stations with multiple monitors. Preliminary support for multiple GPUs was also added on Wayland."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.21.0.md:144
msgid "Apart from the numerous improvements in stability, there are quite a few Plasma components that are getting much better support in Wayland. KRunner, for example, is now able to list all open windows in Wayland, a new component in the panel's system tray informs you of the keyboard layout, and we now support features required for GTK 4, so all GTK 4 applications will now work."
msgstr ""

