#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.22.90.md:20
msgid "This is the Beta release of Plasma - 25th Anniversary Edition. To make sure that end-users have the best possible experience with the next version of Plasma, KDE is releasing today this test version of the software. We encourage the more adventurous to test-run it and report problems so that developers may iron out the wrinkles before the final release scheduled for the 12th of October."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.22.90.md:22
msgid "Plasma 25th Anniversary Edition is a leap forward in the quest for a more performant and usable desktop. We have improved the speed and stability of Plasma, while including changes that make it easier to use both on desktop and touch-enabled devices."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/5/5.22.90.md:24
msgid "**DISCLAIMER:** This is beta software and is released for testing purposes. You are advised to NOT use Plasma 25th Anniversary Edition Beta in a production environment or as your daily desktop. If you do install Plasma 25th Anniversary Edition Beta, you must be prepared to encounter (and [report to the creators](https://bugs.kde.org/)) bugs that may interfere with your day-to-day use of your computer."
