#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:10
msgid "Here are the major changes available in the Plasma 6.1 beta:"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:12
msgid "Triple buffering in KWin for smoother rendering and animations"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:13
msgid "Support for the Wayland Explicit Sync protocol, which should improve life for NVIDIA users in particular"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:14
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Add support for flatpak portals"
msgid "Support for the Input Capture portal"
msgstr "Engadir compatibilidade con portais de Flatpak"

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:15
msgid "Remote Desktop system integration to allow RDP clients to connect to Plasma desktops, plus a new page in System Settings for configuring this"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:16
msgid "New UX for Plasma's edit mode to make its modality more obvious and visually fancier"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:17
msgid "Added a configurable edge barrier between screens, to make it easier to hit UI elements touching the edges between screens. This also allows auto-hide panels on edges between screens to work properly"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:18
msgid "Fake session restore on Wayland that at least re-opens apps that were open last time, even if they don't get positioned in the same place. Support for real session restore is still being worked on"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:19
msgid "Support for syncing the color of your keyboard's RGB backlight with Plasma's accent color"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:20
msgid "Support for using the color profile embedded into the display, for displays that bundle these"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:21
msgid "Support in Discover for replacing end-of-support Flatpak apps with their replacements"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:22
msgid "Support for the battery conservation mode features on many Lenovo IdeaPad and Legion laptops"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:23
msgid "Support for passwordless screen locking, for using it as a screensaver in an environment without security concerns"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:24
msgid "You can now middle-click the Power & Battery widget to block and unblock automatic sleep and screen locking, and scroll over it to switch the active power profile"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:25
msgid "Slightly rounder corners, and more consistency between corner radius everywhere"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:26
msgid "Better window layout algorithm for Overview"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:27
msgid "The \"Shake cursor to find it\" effect has been enabled by default"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:28
msgid "New off-by-default effect to hide the mouse pointer after a period of inactivity"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.0.90.md:29
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "The Mouse System Settings page has been rewritten for libinput support on X and Wayland."
msgid "System Settings Keyboard page has been rewritten in QML"
msgstr "A páxina de configuración dos ratos reescribiuse para compatibilidade con libinput en X e Wayland."

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:22
msgid "Plasma 6 hits its stride with version 6.1. While Plasma 6.0 was all about getting the migration to the underlying Qt 6 frameworks correct (and what a massive job that was), 6.1 is where developers start implementing the features that will take your desktop to a new level."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:27
msgid "In this release, you will find features that go far beyond subtle changes to themes and tweaks to animations (although there is plenty of those too), as you delve into interacting with desktops on remote machines, become more productive with usability and accessibility enhancements galore, and discover customizations that will even affect the hardware of your computer."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:33
msgid "These features and more are being built directly into Plasma's Wayland version natively, avoiding the need for third party software and hacky extensions required by similar solutions implemented in X."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:37
msgid "Things will only get more interesting from here. But meanwhile enjoy what will land on your desktop with your next update."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:42
msgid "**Note:** Due to unforeseen circumstances, we have been unable to ship the new wallpaper, \"Reef\", with this version of Plasma. However, there will be a new wallpaper coming soon in the next 6.2 version."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:46
msgid "If you can't wait, you can **[download \"Reef\" here](https://cdn.kde.org/promo/Announcements/Plasma/6.1/Reef.png)**."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:48
msgid "We apologise for this delay and the inconvenience this may cause."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:58
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Plasma Next"
msgid "Access Remote Plasma Desktops"
msgstr "Plasma Next"

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:60
msgid "One of the more spectacular (and useful) features added in Plasma 6.1 is that you can now start up a remote desktop directly from the *System Settings* app. This means that if you are sysadmin who needs to troubleshoot users' machines, or simply need to work on a Plasma-enabled computer that is out of reach, setting up a connection is just a few clicks away."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:72
msgid "Once enabled, you can connect to the remote desktop using a client such as [KRDC](https://apps.kde.org/krdc/). You will see the remote machine's Plasma desktop in a window and be able to interact with it from your own computer."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:76
msgid "Customization made (more) Visual"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:78
msgid "We all love customizing our Plasma desktops, don't we? One of the quickest ways to do this is by entering Plasma's *Edit Mode* (right-click anywhere on the desktop background and select *Enter Edit Mode* from the menu)."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:84
msgid "In version 6.1, the visual aspect of *Edit Mode* has been overhauled and you will now see a slick animation when you activate it. The entire desktop zooms out smoothly, giving you a better overview of what is going on and allowing you to make your changes with ease."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:89
msgid "Persistent Apps"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:91
msgid "Plasma 6.1 on Wayland now has a feature that \"remembers\" what you were doing in your last session like it did under X11. Although this is still work in progress, If you log off and shut down your computer with a dozen open windows, Plasma will now open them for you the next time you power up your desktop, making it faster and easier to get back to what you were doing."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:99
msgid "Sync your Keyboard's Colored LEDs"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:101
msgid "It wouldn't be a new Plasma release without at least one fancy aesthetic customization features. This time, however, we give you the power to reach beyond the screen, all the way onto your keyboard, as you can now synchronize the LED colours of your keys to match the accent colour on your desktop."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:108
msgid "The ultimate enhancement for the fashion-conscious user."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:110
msgid "*Please note that this feature will not work on unsupported keyboards — support for additional keyboards is on the way!*"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:118
msgid "We have simplified the choices you see when you try to exit Plasma by reducing the number of confusing options. For example, when you press *Shutdown*, Plasma will only list *Shutdown* and *Cancel*, not every single power option."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:122
msgid "**Screen Locking** gives you the option of configuring it to behave like a traditional screensaver, as you can choose it not to ask you for a password to unlock it."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:125
msgid "Two visual accessibility changes make it easier to use the cursor in Plasma 6.1:"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:127
msgid "**Shake Cursor** makes the cursor grow when you \"shake\" it. This helps you locate that tiny little arrow on your large, cluttered screens when you lose it among all those windows."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:131
msgid "**Edge Barrier** is useful if you have a multi-monitor setup and want to access things on the very edge of your monitor. The \"barrier\" is a sticky area for your cursor near the edge between screens, and it makes it easier to click on things (if that is what you want to do), rather than having the cursor scooting across to the next display."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:138
msgid "Two major Wayland breakthroughs will greatly improve your Plasma experience:"
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:140
msgid "**Explicit Sync** eliminates flickering and glitches traditionally experienced by NVidia users."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:143
msgid "**Triple Buffering** support in Wayland makes animations and screen rendering smoother."
msgstr ""

#. +> trunk5
#: content/announcements/plasma/6/6.1.0.md:149
msgid "…and there's much more going on. To see the full list of changes, [check out the changelog for Plasma 6.1](/announcements/changelogs/plasma/6/6.0.5-6.1.0)."
msgstr ""

